000100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000200 PROGRAM-ID. CLASSCND.
000300* The class condition, II-43. NUMERIC is true when the item's
000400* characters are all digits, with a valid operational sign if the
000500* description says there is one and none if it does not.
000600* ALPHABETIC is true when they are all A-Z or space. Both need a
000700* USAGE DISPLAY operand.
000800*
000900* One TRT does each test: a table of zeros for the acceptable
001000* characters and X'FF' elsewhere, and CC=0 means the whole field
001100* was acceptable.
001200 DATA DIVISION.
